{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3010","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3010","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3010\",\"parent_revision\":\"b131eb14000b36a556e81da9bfd7c9d1bf57e68b003bb9833a017680784840c8\",\"root_revision\":\"b131eb14000b36a556e81da9bfd7c9d1bf57e68b003bb9833a017680784840c8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Correction**: this issue originally claimed the `claude-review` check fails because `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is empty. That claim was wrong \u2014 filed from a misread of an unrelated log line without checking the actual failure point. Verified directly against the run logs (2026-08-19):\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml` and `.github/workflows/claude.yml` both authenticate via `claude_code_oauth_token: ${{ secrets.CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN }}` \u2014 not `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` at all.\\n- The `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: ` empty line appears only in a later, unrelated step (\\\"Post buffered inline comments\\\", a bun script that reads that env var but doesn't need it here) \u2014 that step completed successfully (`No buffered inline comments\\\", outcome=success).\\n- The actual failure (run 32206582056, PR #3008, 2026-08-19T01:53:52Z): Claude Code authenticated and initialized correctly with the OAuth token, ran 2 turns over 13.5s ($0.33 cost), then the action's own result reported `\\\"subtype\\\": \\\"success\\\", \\\"is_error\\\": true\\\"` \u2014 an internal execution error inside the Claude Code run itself, not an auth/secret problem.\\n- **This is intermittent, not consistent**: a later run on the same PR (32208279555, ~28 min after) succeeded with the identical secret configuration.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `.github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml` uploads the action's `execution_file` output (`claude-execution-output.json`) as a build artifact on failure (`actions/upload-artifact@v4`, `if: failure()`) so the `result` field \u2014 where the actual error lives when `is_error: true` with `subtype: success` \u2014 is captured instead of discarded\\n- [ ] Once captured on a real failure, identify the specific root cause from the artifact's `result` field (permission denial, plugin result-extraction failure, transient API error, etc.)\\n- [ ] Determine whether the identified cause needs a fix or is acceptable transient-failure behavior for an LLM-driven review action\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer relying on automated Claude Code review**, I want to **understand why claude-code-action's review runs sometimes fail**, so that **PR review coverage is reliable, not intermittent**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Originally misdiagnosed 2026-08-19 from a partial log read; corrected same day after reading the full run logs directly (`gh run view 32206582056 --log-failed`).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research Fact Checked Primary Sources Cited See Issue Comments\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`is_error: true` with `subtype: success` is a protocol-level-success / application-level-failure state \u2014 the CLI exited cleanly but the invoked task failed, and the actual error message lives in the JSON response's `result` field, not `subtype`. Corroborated by Anthropic's Agent SDK structured-outputs docs, a matching upstream SDK issue, and `claude-code-action`'s own `action.yml` (`execution_file` output). The workflow currently discards this file instead of capturing it, so the specific root cause is currently undiagnosable \u2014 hence the acceptance criteria above are \\\"capture the data\\\" first, \\\"diagnose from it\\\" second, not a direct fix.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"86e8a3e5ba104225dfc3b8ff444cc720a85b91d7398688860f0dda71d91d9fa6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPiIZkQ\"}"}